# MoulConfig's render context reaches into GuiGraphicsExtractor to manage the scissor stack and
# to draw. Those members are private, so without widening them here the settings screen throws
# IllegalAccessError the moment it is drawn. SkyHanni widens the same set, which is why the
# crash only shows up on setups that do not have SkyHanni installed.
